    },
    {
        "text": "Theresa goes in deeper, without looking back, until every memory is taken apart into a mess of disconnected white threads."
    },
    {
        "text": "Like the very night, a long time ago, when she was still young, teaching herself to sew with Theresis by her side."
    },
    {
        "text": "The memories disintegrate until a mere fragment of the soul remains."
    },
    {
        "text": "A silhouette stands at the end of that memory. Theresa thinks the figure both familiar and strange."
    },
    {
        "text": "It's the Doctor. It's not the Doctor."
    },
